MODULE: RepairCursorOnlyAfterCompletionFailedCheckpoint
TARGET: RepairCursorOnlyAfterCompletion
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: A failed repair or checkpoint retains an uncommitted cursor.
PERTURBS: FailRepair
--- FIND
    /\ busy' = FALSE /\ selected' = 0 /\ failureUsed' = TRUE /\ work' = 0
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, cursor, dirty, baseline, fingerprint, pendingBaseline,
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: failed completion still consumes the tree.
    /\ busy' = FALSE /\ selected' = 0 /\ failureUsed' = TRUE /\ work' = 0
    /\ cursor' = cursor + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, dirty, baseline, fingerprint, pendingBaseline,
--- END
